{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roboflow/inference/pulls/2737","id":4177587598,"node_id":"PR_kwDOKB1UWs75AO2O","html_url":"https://github.com/roboflow/inference/pull/2737","diff_url":"https://github.com/roboflow/inference/pull/2737.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/roboflow/inference/pull/2737.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roboflow/inference/issues/2737","number":2737,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Workflows resources discovery and models-pre loading","user":{"login":"PawelPeczek-Roboflow","id":146137186,"node_id":"U_kgDOCLXgYg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/146137186?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PawelPeczek-Roboflow","html_url":"https://github.com/PawelPeczek-Roboflow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PawelPeczek-Roboflow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PawelPeczek-Roboflow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PawelPeczek-Roboflow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PawelPeczek-Roboflow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PawelPeczek-Roboflow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PawelPeczek-Roboflow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PawelPeczek-Roboflow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PawelPeczek-Roboflow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PawelPeczek-Roboflow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## What does this PR do?\r\n\r\nThis PR introduces dependent-resources discovery for Workflows: block manifests gain an instance method discover_dependent_resources() returning an EE-regulated, serializable envelope (roboflow_platform_model / roboflow_platform_project / third_party_model, each with a typed pydantic metadata entity). Declarations state the nature of usage — required_action (access vs execution) and execution_location (local / remote / environment_defined) — return None when a block does not declare its dependencies (distinct from [] — declares none), report workflow selectors verbatim with a requires_runtime_resolution() helper, and mirror exactly the model id that run() loads (including synthesized ids such as clip/<version>). All core blocks referencing models, Roboflow projects, or third-party hosted models implement the method, dynamic (custom python) blocks honestly report None, and a repo-wide guard test enforces that every manifest with model/project-kind fields declares its dependencies.\r\n\r\nOn top of that, the PR adds opt-in pre-loading: ExecutionEngine.init(...) accepts dependencies_pre_init (only roboflow_platform_model supported for now), which registers concretely-declared models in the model manager at init time and resolves $inputs-fed model ids once, on the first run — honouring the effective step execution mode, so nothing is fetched when steps execute remotely. InferencePipeline.init_with_workflow(...) exposes this as the workflows_dependencies_pre_init parameter for predictable video-processing startup. Everything is opt-in (all defaults None), the Execution Engine is bumped to v1.14.0 with a changelog entry, and the block-creation docs describe the new contract.\r\n\r\n**Related Issue(s):** <!-- Link to related issues, e.g., Fixes #123 or Related to #456 -->\r\n\r\n## Type of Change\r\n\r\n<!-- Please select one and delete the others, or describe if Other -->\r\n\r\n- New feature (non-breaking change that adds functionality)\r\n\r\n## Testing\r\n\r\n<!-- Describe how you tested your changes -->\r\n- E2E\r\n- [x] I have tested this change locally\r\n- [x] I have added/updated tests for this change\r\n\r\n**Test details:**\r\n<!-- Describe what tests were added/updated and what they cover -->\r\n\r\n## Checklist\r\n\r\n- [x] My code follows the style guidelines of this project\r\n- [x] I have performed a self-review of my own code\r\n- [x] I have commented my code where necessary, particularly in hard-to-understand areas\r\n- [x] My changes generate no new warnings or errors\r\n- [x] I have updated the documentation accordingly (if applicable)\r\n\r\n## Additional Context\r\n\r\n<!-- Add any other context, screenshots, or notes about the PR here -->\r\n","created_at":"2026-07-31T12:14:25Z","updated_at":"2026-07-31T17:13:52Z","closed_at":"2026-07-31T17:13:50Z","merged_at":"2026-07-31T17:13:50Z","merge_commit_sha":"b93d773ce47f8308a6d286a369ad863da268d67c","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[{"login":"hansent","id":137617,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzNzYxNw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/137617?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hansent","html_url":"https://github.com/hansent","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hansent/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hansent/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hansent/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hansent/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hansent/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hansent/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hansent/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hansent/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hansent/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},{"login":"yeldarby","id":870796,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MDc5Ng==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/870796?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/yeldarby","html_url":"https://github.com/yeldarby","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yeldarby/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yeldarby/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yeldarby/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yeldarby/starred{/owner}{/r